 the editable checkout for agent-workspace code, incidental[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]log strings no longer veto recovery, the at-most-once ledger key is[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]derived correctly for day-sharded artifact layouts, and launcher [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]rows that died before naming get a working relaunch path.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]3[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202611/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]auto_restart_update_skew_fixes.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202611/auto_restart_update_skew_fixes.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-1se[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-1se/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]sase-core: managed-root precedence and exception-scoped [/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]never-restart markers[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]core-origin-precedence[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-origin-precedence: in sase-core, a traceback file under a managed [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]root counts as managed origin even when the agent workspace contains [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]that root (self-hosted editable installs), and never-restart markers are[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]scanned over exception text instead of the raw log tail whenever [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]exception evidence exists.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Healer ledger keys derive the project from the canonical [/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]artifact path parser[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]ledger-project-key[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]ledger-project-key: `_target_for_artifacts_dir` derives the ledger [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]project via `parse_agent_artifact_path` instead of `parents[1].name`, so[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]day-sharded ace-run rows key as `<project>__<lineage>` and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]at-most-once guarantee holds across both healer enumeration sources.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Healer relaunches launcher rows that died before naming[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]launcher-relaunch[dim] · [dim][/dim]after ledger-project-key[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]launcher-relaunch: the healer detects failed rows whose runner died [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]before assigning a name (ace-run bootstrap deaths), and relaunches them [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]by resubmitting the row's raw_prompt.md through the existing launch [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]machinery instead of deferring forever on `plan_agent_restart` name [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]lookup.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Ratchet the core pin, align sase tests and docs, replay the [/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]incident[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]pin-docs-verify[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-origin-precedence, ledger-project-key, [/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#AF87FF][dim]launcher-relaunch[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]pin-docs-verify: move sase's sase-core-revision.txt past the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-origin-precedence commit, update sase-side tests that assert the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]old classifier verdicts, refresh docs/reference/agent-auto-restart.md, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and verify with a read-only `sase agent auto-restart scan` replay of the[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]2026-11-12 sase@22e1ef1 episode.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-1se","llm_provider":"muse","model":"muse-spark